and for n even, the k=n/2 term contributes x.

An alternative recursive closed form: 
∫ sinh^n x dx = (1/n) sinh^{n-1} x cosh x - ((n-1)/n) ∫ sinh^{n-2} x dx.

This is a clean recurrence; and its iterated form:
∫₀^x sinh^n = [ (1/n) sinh^{n-1} x cosh x ] + ... 

